{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"367","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Sereja and Algorithm "}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sereja loves all sorts of algorithms. He has recently come up with a new algorithm, which receives a string as an input. Let's represent the input string of the algorithm as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q = q1q2... qk"},{"kind":"text","text":". The algorithm consists of two steps:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Find any continuous subsequence (substring) of three characters of string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":", which doesn't equal to either string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"zyx"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"xzy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yxz"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" doesn't contain any such subsequence, terminate the algorithm, otherwise go to step 2. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Rearrange the letters of the found subsequence randomly and go to step 1. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sereja thinks that the algorithm works correctly on string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" if there is a non-zero probability that the algorithm will be terminated. But if the algorithm anyway will work for infinitely long on a string, then we consider the algorithm to work incorrectly on this string."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sereja wants to test his algorithm. For that, he has string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s = s1s2... sn"},{"kind":"text","text":", consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters. The boy conducts a series of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" tests. As the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th test, he sends substring "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"slisli + 1... sri"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ li ≤ ri ≤ n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the algorithm input. Unfortunately, the implementation of his algorithm works too long, so Sereja asked you to help. For each test "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(li, ri)"},{"kind":"text","text":" determine if the algorithm works correctly on this test or not."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains non-empty string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":", its length ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":") doesn't exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"105"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is guaranteed that string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" only contains characters: '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ m ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of tests. Next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain the tests. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line contains a pair of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ li ≤ ri ≤ n)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes) if the algorithm works correctly on the corresponding test and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes) otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"zyxxxxxxyyz\n5\n5 5\n1 3\n1 11\n1 4\n3 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"YES\nYES\nNO\nYES\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, in test one and two the algorithm will always be terminated in one step. In the fourth test you can get string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"xzyx"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" on which the algorithm will terminate. In all other tests the algorithm doesn't work correctly. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"367A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/367/problem/A"}